      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism argues that the Constitution should be interpreted based on the public understanding of its text at the time it was adopted or, in the case of subsequent amendments, the public understanding at the time of the enactment. Proponents believe this approach limits the judge's personal policy preferences, ensuring the Constitution is a fixed rule of law, not a political opinion. This perspective strongly emphasizes the \"law as a ground for the political,\" favoring the original meaning to maintain constitutional fidelity.",
