      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A strong critique is that \"original meaning\" is inherently unstable and often subjective, as determining the precise 18th or 19th-century *understanding* of complex legal terms is incredibly difficult, if not impossible. Opponents argue that constitutional meaning inherently \"evolves\" to address novel societal problems the framers could not have anticipated. This \"living constitutionalism\" view suggests that a rigid adherence to the past can lead to an anachronistic and unjust application of the law in modern society.",
